# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# This file holds ONLY the database credentials, separately from
# .env.local.example / .env.local, because the Prisma CLI (`prisma db push`,
# `prisma migrate`, etc.) auto-loads a file literally named `.env` and never
# reads `.env.local` — putting DATABASE_URL in .env.local would make every
# `pnpm prisma ...` command fail with "Environment variable not found" even
# after the credential is set, which looks identical to the credential still
# being missing. Next.js and this repo's tests/setup-env.ts both also load
# `.env`, so one file serves the Prisma CLI, the app, and the tests — no
# duplication needed.

# Neon Postgres. DATABASE_URL is the POOLED connection string (host contains
# "-pooler") and is the only credential Prisma 7 needs: prisma.config.ts's
# `datasource.url` and src/leads/store.ts's `pg` Pool (via @prisma/adapter-pg)
# both read it directly. Prisma 6 also wanted DIRECT_DATABASE_URL (the
# non-pooler connection) because `prisma migrate` cannot run advisory locks
# over a pooled connection -- but this project has never had a
# prisma/migrations directory, only ever `prisma db push`, which works fine
# over the pooled connection through the driver adapter. No direct/non-pooler
# variable is needed here.
DATABASE_URL=

# Optional, default OFF -- leave unset. Set to `1` only if you see this exact
# symptom: connections to a dual-stack Postgres host (Neon's pooler, for
# instance) time out even though the host is reachable (e.g. connecting
# directly to one of its resolved IPv4 addresses, instead of the hostname,
# succeeds immediately). That symptom means the runtime has no IPv6 route at
# all, and Node's Happy Eyeballs (RFC 8305) address racing is spuriously
# timing out the IPv4 attempt instead of just failing the unreachable IPv6
# ones and falling back. Setting this disables that racing process-wide.
# Anywhere IPv6 actually works -- which includes Vercel's dual-stack
# functions -- leave it unset: racing addresses is the correct, faster
# behaviour there. See src/leads/env.ts.
DB_DISABLE_HAPPY_EYEBALLS=
